# Copy to .env (gitignored) and edit. Read on import of doc_analysis; a variable
# already set in your shell wins, so CI and one-off overrides still work.

# The LaTeX document repo this analysis writes figures and tables into. Must contain
# Chapters/. Required — every save raises with this name if it is missing.
DOC_REPO=/path/to/my-document

# Where interactive HTML exports and figures_manifest.json go. Every figure is recorded
# in the manifest whichever backend drew it, so on matplotlib this directory holds the
# manifest and nothing else. Optional; defaults to this repo's figures_html/.
# FIGURES_HTML_DIR=/path/to/figures_html

# ---- if you installed the `publish` extra -----------------------------------------
# doc-publish resolves its settings exactly as this package does — real environment
# variable, then $DOC_ENV, then the nearest .env above the working directory — so run
# from this checkout it reads THIS file. Its own settings are not listed here on
# purpose: doc-publish owns that list, and a copy kept in a template drifts from it.
#
# `doc-publish env` appends nothing and overwrites nothing; run here it audits this
# file and names the settings its commands still need. `doc-publish config` then prints
# how every one resolved and from where — the fastest way to find out why a publish
# command cannot see a setting.
#
# Both tools search upward, so one .env in a directory above both checkouts serves
# both. Set DOC_ENV to name that file explicitly if you would rather not rely on the
# search.
